DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->operators->undefine('+','-','*','/');

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`18+9-6+13`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('34'),width=>5}
---

What is the value of [`18+3-10+13`]? [_____]{24}
---

What is the value of [`5+7-11+16/19`]? [_____]{Real(1.84210526316)}
---

What is the value of [`8+18+18-14*19`]? [_____]{Formula('-222')}
---

What is the value of [`12/14+0/8`]? [_____]{Real(0.857142857143)}
---

What is the value of [`1+0/5`]? [_____]{Real(1.)}
---

[`13+18-11+9/19`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>20.4736842105,width=>9}
---

What is the value of [`5+17+12+14/18`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('34.7777777778'),width=>6}
---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
